@startuml workspace-inspection
skinparam backgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 17
skinparam shadowing false
hide footbox
title First-use protected paths — measured macOS 26.5 / 25F71
participant "Signed GUI probe" as Probe
participant "macOS metadata / Launch Services" as Native
actor "VM operator" as Operator
note over Probe,Native
Each case starts with probe consent reset and no TCC rows.
Desktop, Documents and Downloads; own responsible process.
end note
Probe -> Native: stat / symlinks / resource metadata\nbundle identity / registered app
Native --> Probe: values or ENOENT; no consent prompt
Probe -> Native: default-handler lookup for a text file
Native -> Operator: Files and Folders consent dialog
Operator --> Native: Don't Allow
Native --> Probe: TextEdit URL despite denied consent
note over Probe,Native
A returned handler does not prove prompt-free inspection.
Protected default opening and handler reads remain pending.
Named-app selection and reveal do not need this lookup.
No new consent or entitlement is approved by the probe.
Removable/network volumes: unavailable, not passed.
end note
@enduml
